I have two questions about the games listed in the Subject.  I will be
checking the newsgroup every so often, but personal replies are also
welcome.

1)  On a UNIX machine, we have a copy of Omega, and I think it was the
	second one to come out.  I like the game, but it seems that it
	moves really slow, like it takes a half a second to a full second
	to process one move.  Also, the whole bottom half of the city is
	not lit, and has to be mapped out fully by my character.  The first
	version I remember was not like this.  Is the the way it's supposed
	to be?  The slowness is aggravating.

2)  Is there a version of Tetris for the IBM?  I have the Mac version, but
	I think my mom would like the game, but we only have an IBM 
	compatible at home.  How can I get it?  And can someone tell me
	how to get the source for Tetris for UNIX?  If you can send it to
	me, write me a note before you send it, so I can let you know  if
	I already got it or what...don't want 15 copies of the source
	coming in at once.

					Carole and Arnie

